00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.880
Jack: So, what are the roles in
coding teams and software development

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.420
Leah: Project Managers are
responsible for budgets, risk,

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.410
scheduling and contract management.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.699
They might not know the product
that they are creating that well,

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.570
but they are in control overall.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.089
Jack: Product Owners are more
or less analysts and concentrate

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.490
on a product and its features.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.240
Leah: Team Lead is the role given to a
developer with leadership qualities and

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.210
who can maintain communication between
remote development teams and clients.

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:32.420
Jack: Tech Lead has the greatest
knowledge and can solve problems not

00:00:32.429 --> 00:00:35.710
linked with the development, they
are also known as the 'architect'.

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:41.610
Leah: Full Stack Developer is a programmer
not specialised in one area but has a

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:46.140
broad range of skills and can implement
a solution on every architectural layer.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.270
Jack: Front End developers are the point
of contact between the end client or

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.580
user and the system being developed.

00:00:54.709 --> 00:00:57.320
Leah: Back End Developer is the
programmer focused mainly on

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.210
developing logic and data layers.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.080
Jack: QA Lead is responsible for
building the quality assurance team

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:08.549
and its management and is accountable
for relations between QA team members.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.899
Leah: QA engineer is responsible for
preparing tools that allow for automating

00:01:13.899 --> 00:01:16.300
processes to verify software quality.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.110
Jack: Testers are responsible
for conducting manual tests

00:01:20.139 --> 00:01:21.640
doing system verification.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.300
They will try alternate paths
to help eliminate any errors.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.259
Leah: UI Designers are responsible
for preparing, designing the

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:34.270
user interface and transferring
content, style, and graphics.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.839
Jack: UX Designers are responsible
for the users experience analysing

00:01:38.849 --> 00:01:42.520
user behaviour and changing human
computer interaction methods.

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:45.920
Leah: There are two different
approaches to coding teams and

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.710
methods for conducting projects.

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:48.650
One is a 'traditional' development
team and the other is a 'scrum' team.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:56.779
A traditional development teams is
based on a hierarchy between team roles,

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:58.960
so there are leaders and managers.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.500
This allows the project manager
control and it's always clear who

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.190
is responsible for making decisions.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.530
Jack: In a 'scrum' development
team there isn't an organisational

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:11.329
leader, it is self-managed.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.830
Team roles don't overlap, and team members
decide work principles on their own,

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.380
giving a degree of autonomy, which can
help make the experience more enjoyable.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:24.840
However, even though a scrum team
is self-managing, the structure in

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.510
place, ensures, that there is a person
responsible, the 'scrum master' for

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:33.609
the right flow of the project and
that everyone in the team is on track.

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:36.990
Leah: So why is teamwork
important in coding?

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:41.720
When team members work together
effectively towards a common goal like

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.990
developing a product, this will provide
the best experience for end users.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:50.789
Developers, quality assurance personnel
and software testers should all

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:55.279
work closely together as this can
help to increase efficiency, enhance

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.859
creativity as well as drive innovation.

00:02:58.559 --> 00:03:02.859
It can also help to get a product
to market faster and prevent coding

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.650
and other development mistakes.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.070
Jack: When team members feel comfortable
expressing themselves, they can gain more

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:13.200
confidence in expressing and introducing
new ideas, concepts and approaches.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.760
This can encourage creativity which may
result in innovations that may not have

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.299
been thought of in the planning stage.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.269
Leah: When teams don't work well
together, team members will be more

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:27.029
inclined to follow their own goals or
show a lack of commitment to a project.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:31.420
The fear of conflict or avoidance
of accountability may lead to

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.550
trust issues and prevent team
members from sharing ideas.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:38.870
So, it's important for teams to work
on their skills of communication and

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:42.920
collaboration to support efficiency,
creativity, and innovation.

